---@class posthog.external_data_sources.ExternalDataSourceBulkUpdateSchema
---@field id? string Schema identifier to update.
---@field should_sync? boolean Whether the schema should be queryable/synced.
---@field sync_type? posthog.external_data_sources.ExternalDataSchemaSyncTypeEnum|string|distilled.Null Requested sync mode for the schema (incremental, full_refresh, append, cdc, or xmin). * `full_refresh` - full_refresh * `incremental` - incremental * `append` - append * `webhook` - webhook * `cdc` - cdc * `xmin` - xmin
---@field incremental_field? string|distilled.Null Incremental cursor field for incremental or append syncs.
---@field incremental_field_type? string|distilled.Null Type of the incremental cursor field.
---@field sync_frequency? string|distilled.Null Human-readable sync frequency value.
---@field sync_time_of_day? string|distilled.Null UTC anchor time for scheduled syncs.
---@field full_refresh_interval_days? number|distilled.Null Days between scheduled full refreshes, from 1 to 90, or null for none. A full refresh wipes the table and re-imports every row. Re-imported rows count toward usage, and workflows and destinations that run on new rows of the table run again for every row. Incremental, append, and xmin syncs only, and never shorter than the sync frequency.
---@field full_refresh_time_of_day? string|distilled.Null UTC time of day (HH:MM:SS) that scheduled full refreshes are due, for example outside working hours. The refresh runs on the first scheduled sync from up to an hour before this time, so on a table that syncs every few hours it can run hours later. Each interval counts from the slot of this time that the last refresh or save served, where a slot less than an hour away counts as served. Saving a new time restarts the clock, so the first refresh after a save can come up to a day before a full interval has passed. Null counts the interval from when it was saved or from the last full resync. Cleared when full_refresh_interval_days is null.
---@field primary_key_columns? posthog.external_data_sources.ExternalDataSourceBulkUpdateSchemaPrimaryKeyColumnsList|distilled.Null Column names for primary key deduplication.
---@field cdc_table_mode? posthog.external_data_sources.CdcTableModeEnum|string|distilled.Null How CDC-backed tables should be exposed. * `consolidated` - consolidated * `cdc_only` - cdc_only * `both` - both
---@field enabled_columns? posthog.external_data_sources.ExternalDataSourceBulkUpdateSchemaEnabledColumnsList|distilled.Null Columns to sync. Null means sync all columns.
---@field masked_columns? posthog.external_data_sources.ExternalDataSourceBulkUpdateSchemaMaskedColumnsList|distilled.Null Columns whose values are replaced with a one-way digest at sync time. Null means mask nothing. Any change starts a full resync of the table.
---@field row_filters? posthog.external_data_sources.ExternalDataSourceBulkUpdateSchemaRowFiltersList|distilled.Null Row-filter predicates ANDed onto the source query. Null/empty means sync all rows.
---@field apply_sync_defaults? boolean When true and the schema has no sync method configured yet (and this update does not set one), discover the table on the source and fill in default sync settings: incremental sync with an auto-selected tracking column where supported, otherwise append, otherwise full refresh. Ignored for schemas that already have a sync method.

